{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Three buckets from reading the approved RTL: (1) data bits are sent most significant bit first, not least significant bit first; (2) the parity bit is odd parity (~^hold), not even parity (^hold); (3) the stop state lasts CLKS_PER_BIT/2 cycles, not CLKS_PER_BIT. There is one repro testbench per bucket, and each checks only its own behaviour. Reproduction on the simulator is pending the platform's simulator.run gate.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "triage_report", "title": "Triage of the three failing uart_frame_tx nightly tests", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-94eee275db]. The VeriTriage session [run:run-0001] over data_byte_fail.log, parity_bit_fail.log and frame_period_fail.log returned unknown_failure at 30% confidence with 3 evidence nodes and a top hypothesis of 'Likely RTL bug'. That is a lead, not a bucket. A single session over all three logs can also hide a class that one log alone would show. The buckets below therefore come from reading the approved RTL [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], which has an independent review record [evidence:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.e1]. BUCKET data_byte (signature: data field bit order; log data_byte_fail.log): the header comment requires data bits least significant first. START loads tx <= hold[7], and DATA sends hold[3'd7 - next_idx], so the byte goes out MSB first. Fix: send hold[0] from START and hold[next_idx] from DATA. BUCKET parity_bit (signature: parity field value; log parity_bit_fail.log): the parity wire is ~^hold, which gives odd parity, but the comment and spec require even parity. Fix: parity = ^hold. BUCKET frame_period (signature: stop bit / frame length; log frame_period_fail.log): STOP leaves at clk_cnt == CLKS_PER_BIT/2 - 1, so the stop bit lasts half a bit and the frame is 2 cycles short at CLKS_PER_BIT=4. Fix: use bit_done in STOP. The three causes sit in different code (bit-select expressions, the parity reduction, the STOP terminal count) and do not share a root cause, so none were merged. Repros: tb/repro_data_byte.v, tb/repro_parity_bit.v and tb/repro_frame_period.v. Each one is independent of the other two bugs. The data repro checks only data-bit positions. The parity repro compares the parity slot with the even parity of the sent byte, which does not depend on bit order. The frame repro checks only how long busy stays high. Open items: per-log VeriTriage sessions were not run, and the failures were not rerun to rule out flakiness."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/repro_data_byte.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: data bits sent MSB first", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the data_byte bucket against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], tracing to [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It sends non-palindromic bytes, samples each data bit at mid-bit, and checks that the line carries the byte LSB first. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish.", "entry": "tb_uart_frame_tx_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_parity_bit.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: parity bit is odd instead of even", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the parity_bit bucket against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], tracing to [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It samples the parity slot (bit 9 of the frame) and compares it with the even parity of the byte sent. Bit order does not affect this check. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish.", "entry": "tb_uart_frame_tx_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_frame_period.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: stop bit shorter than one bit period", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the frame_period bucket against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], tracing to [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It counts the cycles busy stays high per frame and requires between 11*CLKS_PER_BIT and 12*CLKS_PER_BIT (start + 8 data + parity + stop). It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the