ead of 44). Signature: check frame_period, field busy duration. Suggested fix: compare against CLKS_PER_BIT - 1. The three causes sit in different RTL lines and affect different, independent fields: bit order does not change the parity value or the frame length, and the stop length does not change the sampled data or parity slots. They are therefore kept as three buckets, not merged. Open items: the same-seed rerun that would rule out flakiness has not been recorded; per-log VeriTriage sessions have not been recorded; the log text should be confirmed to match each signature."}], "files": [{"path": "repro_data_byte.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: data bits sent MSB first", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket data_byte of [requirement:req-94eee275db] against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It sends 01, 80, 53 and 0F, samples tx mid-bit in data slots 1..8, and checks the line carries the byte least significant bit first (check data_lsb_first). It counts passed and failed checks and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Expected to fail on the MSB-first ordering identified in the session [run:run-0005]; it does not look at the parity slot or the stop length.", "entry": "tb_uart_frame_tx_repro"}, {"path": "repro_parity_bit.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: parity bit is odd instead of even", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket parity_bit of [requirement:req-94eee275db] against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It sends 00, 01, 03 and FE, samples the parity slot mid-bit, and compares it to ^data, the even-parity value (check parity_even). Because the parity value does not depend on bit order, the MSB-first defect does not affect it. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Lead from [run:run-0005].", "entry": "tb_uart_frame_tx_repro"}, {"path": "repro_frame_period.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro: stop bit shorter than one bit period", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket frame_period of [requirement:req-94eee275db] against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It measures how many clock cycles busy stays high per frame and requires 11*CPB..12*CPB cycles (check frame_period). From reading the RTL, a correct design gives 44 cycles and the half-length stop gives 42. Bit order and parity value do not affect it. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Lead from [run:run-0005].", "entry": "tb_uart_frame_tx_repro"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0005"], "claims": ["From reading the RTL, the data repro should fail on uart_frame_tx_buggy.v because 8'h01 is sent MSB first and read back as 8'h80.", "From reading the RTL, the parity repro should fail on byte 8'h00 because ~^8'h00 = 1 where even parity requires 0.", "From reading the RTL, busy should last 42 cycles per frame in the buggy design and 44 in a design with a full stop bit, at CLKS_PER_BIT=4.", "Each repro is intended to pass on a clean uart_frame_tx and to fail only on its own bucket's defect; the platform's simulator.run gate has not reported on these files yet.", "The mapping of each log to a bucket rests on the log file names and the RTL reading, not on the log contents, which I did not see."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Attempt 1 was refused for naming run:run-0001, which was never recorded. This answer names only run:run-0005, the recorded veritriage.investigate session. The three testbenches keep the same content as the refused attempt; that content was rechecked against the RTL timing (sampling at mid-bit, START at 4 cycles, parity slot at edges 36..40, busy measured as 44 vs 42 cycles). All three share the top module tb_uart_frame_tx_repro, because each runs alone with the approved RTL. Recommended follow-ups before the buckets are final: run veritriage.investigate on each log separately, and rerun each failing test with the same seed."}

